    "content": "901195b1 2025-07-01 flac.md: fix \"-q\" misinformation, and more. (#818)\n* max -q value was wrong, issue xiph#816 . Fixed that.\n* Also, reworded -m, -M for clarity, -p for consistency with -q, --lax for brevity.\n* move the tagging options right after --picture.\n* moved and reworded --no-utf-8 is a tagging option\n* Correct -j description\nCo-authored-by: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>---END---\nf943aa17 2025-03-15 API documentation: replace modules.html by topics.html\nThis fixes the issue reported on\nhttps://lists.xiph.org/pipermail/flac-dev/2025-February/006696.html\n\nNewer Doxygen versions call what was previously api/modules.html\napi/topics.html instead.\n--\n---END---\n6d444f39 2025-06-08 Fix use of uninitialized memory in tests (#828)\nSee https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/827---END---\n8d648456 2025-03-16 Prevent replaygain test from messing up metaflac test (#809)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/806\n\nSee also commit b01e568---END---\n4c578293 2025-02-20 configure.ac: fix bashism (#803)\n'==' is a bashism, use POSIX '=' instead.---END---\n--\nCo-authored-by: Wolfgang Stöggl <c72578@yahoo.de>---END---\n18795be0 2025-01-31 Have \"keep foreign metadata\" note disappear when using --silent (#794)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/792---END---\ncbfe50e3 2025-01-31 Add FLAC__stream_decoder_get_link_lengths (#793)\n---END---\n3542ae8e 2025-01-27 Upgrade an assert to an error\n---END---\n--\n---END---\n3319a88e 2025-01-23 Fix memory allocation failure not being propagated correctly (#789)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A---END---\n426172a1 2025-01-22 Fix version string from git for shallow clone (#788)\nAlso, make msys2 action find git executable---END---\ne1f62ebe 2025-01-21 Fix some more undefined behaviour\nAs https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/784 notified me of\nundefined behaviour going undetected by the fuzzers, I ran the test\nsuite with the full undefined behaviour sanitizer enabled.\n\nThere is one bit of undefined behaviour that I cannot fix,\n--\n---END---\na628cca3 2025-01-17 Remove null pointer arithmetic as it is undefined behaviour\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/784\n\nCo-authored-by: braheezy <11700503+braheezy@users.noreply.github.com>\n---END---\naa414e46 2024-12-29 Limit amount of samples to decode in fuzzer_tool_flac (#783)\n--\n---END---\na8adc6c0 2024-12-27 Check for overflow in off_t when parsing chunks (#781)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42537590---END---\n7f491ae4 2024-12-24 Only call tell callback when necessary (#779)\nThis slightly speeds up the encoder by reducing the number of\nsyscalls, but can result in a 30% speedup in extreme cases, mostly\nwhen using extremely small blocksizes.---END---\n--\nchecked.---END---\nc786b1cd 2024-12-06 Fix another endless loop in chained ogg handling (#772)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A (local run)---END---\n301f655b 2024-12-05 Fix decoder not able to find start of next link (#771)\nSee https://github.com/xiph/flac/pull/765 for report.---END---\nd1d72aa7 2024-12-03 Speed up bitwriter_grow_ by growing exponentially\nGrowing up to the max allowed size took roughly 4000 reallocations,\n--\n---END---\ndca8eafe 2024-12-03 Fix AIFF-C writing without foreign metadata input\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/767\n---END---\n669eae96 2024-12-03 Add roundtrip tests for AIFF-C handling in command line tool\n---END---\nffc5bf56 2024-12-02 Improve fuzzer_seek performance by imposing limits\n--\n---END---\n7e0c04c4 2024-11-29 Fix endless loop when skipping link (#765)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A (local run)---END---\ne3a7157b 2024-11-28 Fix heap overflow under out-of-memory conditions ... (#764)\n... and use realloc of linkdetails more efficiently. This should\nreduce the number of fuzzer timeouts for fuzzer_seek\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/379254072---END---\na0e30a4e 2024-11-12 Don't overwrite abort or out-of-memory with seek error\n---END---\nc98d86d2 2024-11-08 Reset invalid decoder in fuzzer_seek\n---END---\nf2965d2c 2024-11-14 Fix Wave64 foreign metadata application ID (#762)\nSee https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/761---END---\n17811b3a 2024-11-13 Add FLAC__stream_decoder_find_total_samples (#758)\n---END---\necbac1ff 2024-11-12 Help text: corrected raw options (#759)\n---END---\n--\n---END---\nfd09bbb8 2024-10-29 Fix end-of-stream signal not being propagated\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/370597904\n---END---\na7d69df6 2024-10-25 Add option to metaflac to write to different file\n---END---\n73b55024 2024-10-24 Enable libFLAC to write to new file on changing metadata\n--\n---END---\n2a23a2af 2024-10-08 Address signed integer overflow (#751)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42526392---END---\ned4e1c46 2024-10-08 Don't try to skip link after allocation failure (#752)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/371233030---END---\n00a27084 2024-10-07 Free metadata if subsequent allocation fails (#750)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42538223---END---\n86d6de66 2024-10-05 Disable fuzzer_tool_flac for i386 (#749)\nRevert commits ce91056 and 33b9a4a, disable tool_flac fuzzer for\ni386 ASAN because weird bugs keep popping up---END---\n50efa0c8 2024-10-04 Improve allocation of linkdetails, check more often (#748)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/370562609\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/371068253---END---\n40ca8c73 2024-10-04 Only fail on memory allocation after initializing other variables (#747)\nAs this issue was not reproducible, this might not actually be a\nfix.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42538252---END---\na89875d8 2024-09-30 Fix memory leak in flac command line tool (#746)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42538282---END---\ne4f1ee9f 2024-09-30 Fix signed integer overflow in seeking code (#745)\nAlso add some more seeking tests\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/369652821---END---\nb8efde21 2024-09-29 Add two error statuses to the stream decoder for broken files (#744)\n---END---\nd367d6fe 2024-08-28 Bump library version numbers and update ABI dumps\n---END---\n--\nuse the last few years, it is time to remove them.---END---\nd34489c4 2024-08-31 Fix overflow when skipping over raw input (#737)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/655---END---\n4a271d2e 2024-08-30 Add note to metaflac warning about writing to symlinks\n---END---\n685f4f69 2024-08-30 Let libFLAC handle symlinks on metadata handling\nWithout this commit, libFLAC happily overwrites symlinks with\n--\n---END---\n1880f210 2024-08-07 don't just pass 0 for samples in Ogg/FLAC callback\nThis is a fix for https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/661\n---END---\n8e6498d4 2024-08-21 Improve console output of flac tool (#734)\nFixes various cases of erratic behaviour (most notably output not\nstarting on the first character of a line). Also, some warnings\n--\n---END---\ne50c876a 2024-07-25 Do not try to apply replaygain when bps changes\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A\n---END---\n33b9a4a7 2024-07-25 Work around i386 ASAN null pointer bug\nFor some reason, i386 ASAN does not copy a pointer somewhere in the\ncode. Using gdb I get a mention of a synthetic pointer, so perhaps\n--\nisn't necessary otherwise and is only activated for i386 ASAN.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=58524\n---END---\n215d1aa6 2024-07-23 Do not try to apply replaygain when bps < 4 or bps > 24\n---END---\ndefad5b5 2024-07-23 Turn replaygain application off when impossible\n--\nnot actually turn off replaygain application.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=70482\n---END---\n8c244b83 2024-07-17 Add level 0 Ogg reading capability to tests and docs\n---END---\nf94d34ff 2024-07-16 Enable MD5 checking of input when reencoding to stdout\n--\nThis was missed in commit dda3e77---END---\n3468459d 2024-07-14 Fix endless loop in foreign metadata handling (#725)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=58545---END---\nd48b689a 2024-07-12 Enable fuzzing of writing foreign metadata back on decoding\nThe output file was deleted before writing back foreign metadata\ncould take place, making that code always fail and not covered by\nfuzzing\n--\n---END---\n15ea6ef8 2024-07-11 Fix analyze mode trying to get positions from stdin (#720)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=68539---END---\n9977773a 2024-07-10 Address two Clang warnings\n---END---\n09d7887b 2024-07-10 Remove unnecessary assert condition\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=60777\n---END---\ne14acb96 2024-07-04 More Pandoc HTML fixes (#717)\n- Make html manpages build with old pandoc versions\n- Add building of html docs to CMake---END---\nb6b5b325 2024-07-03 Make UTF-8 decoder more restrictive (#712)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/706---END---\nb773157a 2024-06-26 Update 'distcheck' github action to Ubuntu 24.04\n---END---\n97d8cd19 2024-06-26 Add building of a tarball to github actions\n---END---\n--\noutput of non-ASCII characters fails. This commit should fix that.\n\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/713\n\nNOTE: To enable this change, metaflac no longer outputs\napplication block data as binary directly, because that would\npotentially result in incorrect UTF-8 codepoint. Instead, all\nbytes that cannot be represented as printable ASCII are\nreplaced with the Unicode replacement character---END---\n706c0614 2024-06-19 Fix https://github.com/m-ab-s/media-autobuild_suite/issues/2718 (#711)\n---END---\nef1e185e 2024-06-19 test: stop using which (#709)\n`which` is an external command which isn't required by POSIX.\n\n--\n---END---\n04532802 2024-05-02 Escape double dashes, so they don't get converted to em dashes (#698)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/671---END---\nf5012d5e 2024-04-26 Update iconv.m4\n---END---\nd6921ed6 2024-04-26 Fix use of --enable-asm-optimizations\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/686\n---END---\nde803492 2024-05-01 Fix bug in CHECK_ORDER_IS_VALID macro in functions with intrinsics (#696)\nThis fixes a few things I missed with https://github.com/xiph/flac/pull/694---END---\n653b1187 2024-05-01 Update GNU Free Documentation License (#697)\n--\n---END---\n61f8513c 2024-04-30 Fix bug in CHECK_ORDER_IS_VALID macro (#694)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/635\n---END---\n49ab34df 2024-04-22 [CMake] disable fseeko on 32-bit Android before API 24\nIt can be linked in the NDK so check_function_exists detects it. But it's only supporting _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64\nsince Android API 24 [1].\n--\ncondition: encoder->protected_->state is written without a lock.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=62650---END---\nd2b24410 2024-03-09 Different loose mid side algorithm compatible with multithreading (#675)\n---END---\n8d4ccdfb 2024-03-08 Update CMakeLists to allow building with emscripten (#664)\n---END---",
