    "content": "default behaviour remains unchanged.\n---END---\nf47f100d 2025-06-08 Fix android >=24 build with NDK toolchain (#831)\n---END---\n6d444f39 2025-06-08 Fix use of uninitialized memory in tests (#828)\nSee https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/827---END---\n8d648456 2025-03-16 Prevent replaygain test from messing up metaflac test (#809)\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/806\n\nSee also commit b01e568---END---\n4c578293 2025-02-20 configure.ac: fix bashism (#803)\n'==' is a bashism, use POSIX '=' instead.---END---\n018b4aca 2025-02-20 Set metaflac version stdout/stderr to UTF-8 on WIN32 (#812)\nReplace one last call to printf() with flac_printf() that was missed\non commit dda3e77---END---\n--\n30cdb4d3 2024-12-18 Update changelog\n---END---\n163e4a7f 2024-12-18 Update flac.md: Reordering and updating options descriptions & more (#769)\nCo-authored-by: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>---END---\n0ef3a5d8 2024-12-11 Silence a few 'may be used uninitialized' warnings\n---END---\n533257d8 2024-12-11 Update CMake minimum version\nSome subdirectories had a higher minimum version specified. This\nis now 'propagated'. Also, compatibily with newer CMake versions\nis now explicity stated.\n---END---\nc47beb15 2024-12-11 Limit number of rewinds (#773)\nThis should reduce the number of timeouts. In case the decoder\nkeeps rewinding, check 4 of the 8 CRC8 bits. If they match, keep\nrewinding.\n--\n645d651e 2023-04-28 Only unset 'first' after successful execution\n'first' was handed to flac__encode_file on the first file of a\nset, to let that function know replaygain needs to be initialized.\nHowever, when processing of the first file fails, the second file\nuses replaygain uninitialized.\n---END---\n189cbaab 2023-04-28 Only invalidate last seen framesync when actually emptying buffer\nThe last seen framesync in the bitreader was invalidated when\nreading new data in. However, data only leaved the buffer when\nmore than one word has been fully read. When an invalid frame is\nread and reading is aborted within less than a wordlength because\nof reaching end-of-stream, the read_from_client had invalidated\nthe last seen framesync, causing rewinding to the start of the\nbitreader. This causes an infinite loop, syncing on the same\npattern every time.\n--\nac39a007 2023-03-17 Improve fuzzer_tool_metaflac\n---END---\n2568bf69 2023-03-03 Fix metaflac memory leak\n---END---\n5f39e88a 2023-02-17 Fix strlen being used on uninitialized data\n---END---\ncad22e0e 2023-02-23 Prevent strcmp being used on invalid data\n---END---\n67d2e1ee 2023-02-23 Add fuzzer for metaflac command-line tool\n---END---\ne683286b 2023-03-18 Add use of stdin to fuzzer_tool_flac, and redirect stdout\n---END---\n0e1535cc 2023-03-18 Check for invalid blocksize (65536)\n---END---\nf4220895 2023-03-18 Fix null dereference\n--\n---END---\n9382c537 2023-02-22 Add checks on re-encoding FLAC\nWhile decoding from FLAC checks for changes no. of channels, bps\nand sample rate, re-encoding doesn't. A fuzzer found use of\nuninitialized memory because of this. A few checks are added,\nalthough the user isn't warned on a samplerate change.\n---END---\n14f19cb2 2023-02-22 Fix undefined behaviour in chunk size reading\n---END---\nda3254a7 2023-02-22 Fix null dereference read\n---END---\n67a0a153 2023-02-22 Fix oss-build problem and add fuzzer_tool_flac to .gitignore\n---END---\n0408d251 2023-02-22 In metaflac/usage.c, add missing newlines in the --remove-all-tags-except description\n---END---\n--\n69cf76c5 2022-05-20 Fix use of undefined value\nThe mechanism to improve metadata reading added in 0077d3b overrides\na FLAC__STREAM_DECODER_ABORTED with\nFLAC__STREAM_DECODER_SEARCH_FOR_FRAME_SYNC causing the decoder to\noverread a buffer into an uninitialized part. A check is added that\nensures searching for frame sync is only set when the decoder is\nstill in a valid state\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=47525\n---END---\n43b6b64c 2022-05-16 [CMake] Add /arch:avx2 flag, clarify WITH_SSE2 and WITH_AVX options\nAdds /arch:avx2 to the avx2-specific source files. This mirrors the\ncurrent vcxproj files. While it currently brings no improvements,\nit might if CPU-specific optimization is left to the compiler\n--\n- FLAC__STREAM_ENCODER_FRAMING_ERROR\n- FLAC__STREAM_ENCODER_MEMORY_ALLOCATION_ERROR\n\nFLAC__STREAM_ENCODER_CLIENT_ERROR does not trigger an abort because\nit is used to signal invalid input. FLAC__STREAM_ENCODER_UNINITIALIZED\ndoes not trigger an abort because init fails when invalid parameters\nare given\n---END---\n6122337f 2022-05-10 Check whether verify decoder is still valid\nErrors returned by the verifing decoder were ignored, while an error\noften invalidates the assumptions the encoder made about the state\nof the verifying decoder. If an error was ignored, it could be the\ndecoder outputs an (invalid) frame with a different number of channels\nthan the encoder expects. This could cause heap overflows. This\ncommit adds checks for this occuring.\n--\nwarning: format not a string literal and no format arguments [-Wformat-security]\n---END---\n7b73bbcc 2022-02-28 Move initialization of state up in stream_encoder_new\nIn stream_encoder_new, set_defaults_ was called before setting\nencoder->protected_->state to uninitialized. However, this state\nwas being accessed by set_compression_level in set_defaults_. As\nthis is undefined behaviour, move the initialization of\nencoder->protected_->state up to before calling set_default_\n---END---\n4a8ec07e 2022-04-11 Add checks that supplied samples are bounded within bits-per-sample\nThe encoder did not check whether samples provided through\nFLAC__stream_encoder_process or FLAC__stream_encoder_process_interleaved\nwere bounded to fall within the set bits_per_sample (bps). This created\nall kinds of trouble within the encoder, as there are numerous times\nwhere the encoder chooses between different datapaths, data types and\n--\n6c03ab20 2016-01-24 Clean up #includes\nPatch-from: lvqcl <lvqcl.mail@gmail.com>\n---END---\ne0b406f6 2016-01-23 Fix three more cppcheck warnings\n* src/flac/vorbiscomment.c:203: Uninitialized variable: converted.\n* src/flac/vorbiscomment.c:210: Uninitialized variable: converted.\n* src/test_libFLAC++/decoders.cpp:507: Memory leak: decoder.\n---END---\nd908b292 2016-01-22 Fix some cppcheck reports\n* src/libFLAC/metadata_iterators.c:3247: (error) va_list `va` was opened\n  but not closed with va_end().\n* src/share/grabbag/snprintf.c:66: (error) va_list `va` was opened but\n  not closed with va_end().\n* src/utils/flactimer/main.cpp:84: (warning) Either the condition `!fout`\n  is redundant or there is possible null pointer dereference.\n\n--\nc3cf5312 2015-08-01 autogen.sh: Add --no-symlinks option\n---END---\n9e2bf61d 2015-08-01 autogen.sh: Switch from bash to sh and make it POSIX\n---END---\n6ced857c 2015-07-13 libFLAC: Fix decoder_flush with uninitialized decoder\nCloses: https://sourceforge.net/p/flac/bugs/428\n---END---\ncf7442d6 2015-07-12 libFLAC/cpu.c: Assume Android has SSE\nAccording to https://developer.android.com/ndk/guides/abis.html#x86\nAndroid always support SSE, so there's no need to test SSE OS support.\n\nWhy both __ANDROID__ and ANDROID are tested:\nhttp://stackoverflow.com/questions/15328751/android-macro-suddenly-not-defined\nhttp://stackoverflow.com/questions/6374523/how-to-detect-compilation-by-android-ndk-in-a-c-c-file\nhttps://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/android-ndk/cf9_f1SLXls\n--\ned1db1f6 2004-10-14 add --input-size option to flac\n---END---\nc99aa82e 2004-10-07 patch from Steven Richman: adds support for streaming http transport to xmms plugin\n---END---\n076adb03 2004-10-07 fix uninitialized variable\n---END---\n5e8e7339 2004-10-07 minor fixes to comply with C99's new pointer aliasing rules\n---END---\n91b4ce51 2004-10-06 fix #ifdef problems that existed when FLAC__NO_ASM is defined\n---END---\n607fc843 2004-10-06 fix debian bug #274301: libflac4 segfaults on corrupt flac files\n---END---\n53677597 2004-10-01 more path fixes\n---END---\n83688e94 2004-10-01 add explicit path to libogg\n--\n0bb57d0e 2004-07-16 add tests for -f and flac default behavior when the output file already exists\n---END---\nd3ec1c6f 2004-07-16 print error if output file already exists, instead of overwriting by default; add -f (--force) option to force overwriting of files\n---END---\ncc75611f 2004-07-16 fix valgrind uninitialized memory errors\n---END---\n89f161c5 2004-07-16 tempfile only needs to be opened with wb, not w+b\n---END---\nb0be1e87 2004-07-16 remove unused variables\n---END---\n1138520d 2004-07-16 when encoding to Ogg FLAC, set a random serial number (instead of 0) if one is not provided on the command-line\n---END---\ncd5b1a63 2004-07-16 minor comment fixes\n---END---\nd5c593b0 2004-07-16 add documentation for new callback-based functions\n--\n0e46bf56 2004-07-15 do not close any file handles in the callback-based chain reading/writing\n---END---\n0b8b5646 2004-07-15 add tests of mismatched read/write protections in chain interface\n---END---\nb279130e 2004-07-14 fix uninitialized variable error turned up by valgrind\n---END---\n65831dd1 2004-07-14 add tests for callback-based chain reading/writing\n---END---\n028d97ee 2004-07-14 fix bug in FLAC__metadata_chain_check_if_tempfile_needed()\n---END---\n463a22cc 2004-07-11 add callback-based versions of chain writing: FLAC__metadata_chain_check_if_tempfile_needed(), FLAC__metadata_chain_write_with_callbacks(), FLAC__metadata_chain_write_with_callbacks_and_tempfile()\n---END---\neaf8fbd8 2004-07-11 add an EOF callback to the mix\n---END---\n91748beb 2004-07-10 add FLAC__metadata_chain_read_with_callbacks()\n--\nf26386a8 2003-09-03 fix link to nightly CVS tarballs\n---END---\n1ba525b9 2003-09-03 fix rounding bug in buffer size calculation (MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WINDOW)\n---END---\nbef021a1 2003-09-03 fix possibly uninitialized var if a file has no STREAMINFO block\n---END---\n9bb1a16f 2003-08-29 fix typo\n---END---\n9d260d88 2003-08-28 more verbiage about \"make check\"\n---END---\nf1c72d55 2003-08-28 add link to faq.html in navbar\n---END---\n35a0903e 2003-08-28 add FAQ for \"how to use with EAC\"\n---END---\nd7ec1026 2003-08-28 add link to MAREO\n--\n59d84502 2002-12-30 patch from Miroslav\n---END---\n94317e5a 2002-12-30 remove reference to --no-escape-coding\n---END---\n1a28b690 2002-12-29 fix problem with uninitialized data from valgrind\n---END---\n6bc4e4f2 2002-12-29 remove --workaroung-gcc296-bugs=yes from Valgrind invocation\n---END---\ndd190236 2002-12-29 need release bitbuffer even in error cases in write_bitbuffer_()\n---END---\n10240349 2002-12-29 need /GR for dynamic_cast to work for some reason\n---END---\n1dfef453 2002-12-29 minor syntax\n---END---\n92849946 2002-12-28 add Boss Ogg to S/W section\n--\n15d9eba1 2002-12-28 add \"all\" to phony targets\n---END---\nf1f359ed 2002-12-28 minor syntax\n---END---\n45062b84 2002-12-28 fix uninitialized data\n---END---\n8825c571 2002-12-28 fix memory leaks and uninitialized data\n---END---\nf91251d1 2002-12-28 add flushed fwrite in Valgrind mode\n---END---\n8b9a477a 2002-12-28 fix verbiage about get_block() in Iterator class\n---END---\n21cd7b82 2002-12-28 add \"src\" target\n---END---\n05f133c9 2002-12-28 add Makefile.lite\n---END---\nfcd85f83 2002-12-28 initial import\n--\n91d37b24 2002-12-23 fix problem with FLAC_plugin__charset_test_conversion() not returning a value\n---END---\n36f7d0a6 2002-12-23 fix warning about unused vars\n---END---\n709b7fce 2002-12-23 fix uninitialized var\n---END---\n06ecb281 2002-12-23 minor typo\n---END---\n2b7cc17a 2002-12-23 fix problem with recursive use of TESTS_ENVIRONMENT\n---END---\nadcc4a1d 2002-12-21 minor updates\n---END---\neb0ccd64 2002-12-21 fix some typos\n---END---\ne3cd991a 2002-12-21 add metaflac.sgml\n--\n16129499 2002-12-14 add link to foobar2000, audiotron, update codec verbiage\n---END---\n8232e295 2002-12-14 do --ski