    "content": "==== 808efb32\n808efb32 Explicitly check for bps == 0 when applying replaygain\n src/flac/decode.c | 7 +++++++\n 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)\ncommit 808efb328717af811d24a8d59fdcc73f5f328b01\nAuthor: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>\nDate:   Fri May 19 08:12:55 2023 +0200\n\n    Explicitly check for bps == 0 when applying replaygain\n\n    During application of replaygain, bps is checked to be > 0. This\n    should never happen in a valid file. This check is specific for\n    replaygain application instead of more generic (at streaminfo)\n    because we still want to be able to recover files in which\n    streaminfo is invalid or missing.\n\ndiff --git a/src/flac/decode.c b/src/flac/decode.c\nindex d874b4b8..bb39fcd2 100644\n--- a/src/flac/decode.c\n+++ b/src/flac/decode.c\n@@ -1543,6 +1543,13 @@ void metadata_callback(const FLAC__StreamDecoder *decoder, const FLAC__StreamMet\n                                        return;\n                                }\n                        }\n+                       else if(decoder_session->bps == 0) {\n+                               flac__utils_printf(stderr, 1, \"%s: WARNING: can't apply ReplayGain, bit-per-sample value is invalid\\n\", decoder_session->inbasefilename);\n+                               if(decoder_session->treat_warnings_as_errors) {\n+                                       decoder_session->abort_flag = true;\n+                                       return;\n+                               }\n+                       }\n                        else {\n                                const char *ls[] = { \"no\", \"peak\", \"hard\" };\n                                const char *ns[] = { \"no\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\" };\n==== defad5b5\ndefad5b5 Turn replaygain application off when impossible\n src/flac/decode.c | 1 +\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\ncommit defad5b5442550a9bd678076fe7ad125edb9f087\nAuthor: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jul 23 08:24:20 2024 +0200\n\n    Turn replaygain application off when impossible\n\n    Addition to commit 808efb3. That commit threw a warning, but did\n    not actually turn off replaygain application.\n\n    Credit: Oss-Fuzz\n    Issue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=70482\n\ndiff --git a/src/flac/decode.c b/src/flac/decode.c\nindex 6a89b144..099348b6 100644\n--- a/src/flac/decode.c\n+++ b/src/flac/decode.c\n@@ -1590,6 +1590,7 @@ void metadata_callback(const FLAC__StreamDecoder *decoder, const FLAC__StreamMet\n                                        decoder_session->abort_flag = true;\n                                        return;\n                                }\n+                               decoder_session->replaygain.apply = false;\n                        }\n                        else {\n                                const char *ls[] = { \"no\", \"peak\", \"hard\" };\n==== 215d1aa6\n215d1aa6 Do not try to apply replaygain when bps < 4 or bps > 24\n src/flac/decode.c | 8 ++++++++\n 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)\ncommit 215d1aa633b218ae16bfc1b09aed6f3f7a22d19e\nAuthor: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jul 23 08:29:08 2024 +0200\n\n    Do not try to apply replaygain when bps < 4 or bps > 24\n\ndiff --git a/src/flac/decode.c b/src/flac/decode.c\nindex 099348b6..8e73a933 100644\n--- a/src/flac/decode.c\n+++ b/src/flac/decode.c\n@@ -1592,6 +1592,14 @@ void metadata_callback(const FLAC__StreamDecoder *decoder, const FLAC__StreamMet\n                                }\n                                decoder_session->replaygain.apply = false;\n                        }\n+                       else if(decoder_session->bps < 4 || decoder_session->bps > 24) {\n+                               flac__utils_printf(stderr, 1, \"%s: WARNING: can't apply ReplayGain, bit-per-sample value must be between 4 and 24\\n\", decoder_session->inbasefilename);\n+                               if(decoder_session->treat_warnings_as_errors) {\n+                                       decoder_session->abort_flag = true;\n+                                       return;\n+                               }\n+                               decoder_session->replaygain.apply = false;\n+                       }\n                        else {\n                                const char *ls[] = { \"no\", \"peak\", \"hard\" };\n                                const char *ns[] = { \"no\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\" };\n==== e50c876a\ne50c876a Do not try to apply replaygain when bps changes\n src/flac/decode.c | 4 ++++\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)\ncommit e50c876a1c0348c23f26b2ee348a2dee40c9d23b\nAuthor: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Jul 25 12:49:00 2024 +0200\n\n    Do not try to apply replaygain when bps changes\n\n    Credit: Oss-Fuzz\n    Issue: N/A\n\ndiff --git a/src/flac/decode.c b/src/flac/decode.c\nindex 8e73a933..4d7eb310 100644\n--- a/src/flac/decode.c\n+++ b/src/flac/decode.c\n@@ -1154,6 +1154,10 @@ FLAC__StreamDecoderWriteStatus write_callback(const FLAC__StreamDecoder *decoder\n                                flac__utils_printf(stderr, 1, \"%s: ERROR, bits-per-sample is %u in this frame but %u in previous frames\\n\", decoder_session->inbasefilename, bps, decoder_session->bps);\n                        if(!decoder_session->continue_through_decode_errors)\n                                return FLAC__STREAM_DECODER_WRITE_STATUS_ABORT;\n+                       else if(decoder_session->replaygain.apply) {\n+                               flac__utils_printf(stderr, 1, \"%s: ERROR, cannot decode through previous error with replaygain application turned on\\n\", decoder_session->inbasefilename, bps, decoder_session->bps);\n+                               return FLAC__STREAM_DECODER_WRITE_STATUS_ABORT;\n+                       }\n                }\n        }\n        else {\n==== 51e61ae9\n51e61ae9 Fix mistake in fuzzing seed corpus\n oss-fuzz/seedcorpus/fuzzer_tool_flac/replaygain-which-is-not-lossless-ogg.fuzz | Bin 15406 -> 8051 bytes\n oss-fuzz/seedcorpus/fuzzer_tool_flac/replaygain-which-is-not-lossless.fuzz     | Bin 15852 -> 15852 bytes\n 2 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)\ncommit 51e61ae99e574142391ca264fd46e91502bfb5c0\nAuthor: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>\nDate:   Fri Jul 12 09:41:19 2024 +0200\n\n    Fix mistake in fuzzing seed corpus\n\n    The seed corpus had a file that was supposed to cover replaygain\n    synthesis, but didn't have any replaygain tags. Because of the\n    fixed format of these tags, they aren't reasonbly reachable by\n    fuzzing without help\n\ndiff --git a/oss-fuzz/seedcorpus/fuzzer_tool_flac/replaygain-which-is-not-lossless.fuzz b/oss-fuzz/seedcorpus/fuzzer_tool_flac/replaygain-which-is-not-lossless.fuzz\nindex 9d97430b..47d39bf8 100644\nBinary files a/oss-fuzz/seedcorpus/fuzzer_tool_flac/replaygain-which-is-not-lossless.fuzz and b/oss-fuzz/seedcorpus/fuzzer_tool_flac/replaygain-which-is-not-lossless.fuzz differ",
