    "content": "6974998f 2025-02-03 Update copyright to 2025 (#795)\n---END---\n3542ae8e 2025-01-27 Upgrade an assert to an error\n---END---\naa414e46 2024-12-29 Limit amount of samples to decode in fuzzer_tool_flac (#783)\n---END---\ndca8eafe 2024-12-03 Fix AIFF-C writing without foreign metadata input\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/767\n---END---\n7f46eb20 2024-10-29 Fix -Wunused-result warning for ID3v1 detection\n---END---\n08cf8a19 2024-08-23 Improve decoding of chained streams in flac command line tool\n---END---\nfbe98a84 2024-08-20 Add capability to decode chained stream to flac command line tool\n---END---\n--\nFixes various cases of erratic behaviour (most notably output not\nstarting on the first character of a line). Also, some warnings\nand errors now mark the location in the stream where this error\nseems to have occured---END---\ne50c876a 2024-07-25 Do not try to apply replaygain when bps changes\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A\n---END---\n215d1aa6 2024-07-23 Do not try to apply replaygain when bps < 4 or bps > 24\n---END---\ndefad5b5 2024-07-23 Turn replaygain application off when impossible\nAddition to commit 808efb3. That commit threw a warning, but did\nnot actually turn off replaygain application.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=70482\n---END---\nd48b689a 2024-07-12 Enable fuzzing of writing foreign metadata back on decoding\nThe output file was deleted before writing back foreign metadata\ncould take place, making that code always fail and not covered by\nfuzzing\n---END---\nde8bbb0d 2024-07-11 Update copyright to 2024 (#722)\n---END---\n15ea6ef8 2024-07-11 Fix analyze mode trying to get positions from stdin (#720)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=68539---END---\n7acdaabe 2024-06-05 Fix fallback to frame header bps.\nCommit d4daa86167b1 (\"Check for bps% 8 != 0 if no streaminfo is present\")\nbreaks fallback to frame header bps as it tests decoder_session->bps at\na point where it is guaranteed to be 0 as this is the else case of the\nif(decoder_session->bps) block.\n\nSome corrupted FLAC files that used to play before the above mentioned\ncommit no longer can be played.\n\nMove decoder_session->bps = bps to before the decoder_session->bps\n--\nframes turned out to be very large, for framesize 16 these syscalls\ntook over half the execution time. This commit only calls clock()\nwhen at least 10.000 samples have been encoded or 25.000 samples\nhave been decoded since the last call to clock()---END---\n08f8af08 2023-06-18 Improve on \"Check for got_stream_info instead of samplerate being 0\"\nThis improves on commit 6db29d1. It turns that commit broke some\nparsing, this fixes it---END---\ne00d9b88 2023-06-06 Update copyright year and maintainer status\n---END---\n808efb32 2023-05-19 Explicitly check for bps == 0 when applying replaygain\nDuring application of replaygain, bps is checked to be > 0. This\nshould never happen in a valid file. This check is specific for\nreplaygain application instead of more generic (at streaminfo)\nbecause we still want to be able to recover files in which\nstreaminfo is invalid or missing.\n---END---\n946c25de 2023-05-02 Check for overflow when converting skip and until to samples\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=57409\n---END---\nc7861aa8 2023-04-28 Also apply shift to raw data\nThis change only applies when bitdepth changes halfway a stream.\nIt is more a technicality that needs fixing because of fuzzing than\nan actual problem\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=58357\n---END---\nd4daa861 2023-04-23 Check for bps% 8 != 0 if no streaminfo is present\nThis extends commit c671e1c for cases where streaminfo is not\npresent.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=58277\n---END---\n5008827b 2023-04-21 Remove files generated during fuzzing of flac tool\nCI-Fuzz occassionally runs out of disk space, and there might be\nother problems (coverage suddenly vanishing for example) related\nto disk space issues. This commit should make sure all files\ngenerated by the flac tool are removed as soon as they are closed.\n---END---\n798fe376 2023-04-18 Error when skip or until are used on a file without streaminfo\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=58031\n---END---\nf4220895 2023-03-18 Fix null dereference\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=57032\n---END---\n6db29d10 2023-03-08 Check for got_stream_info instead of samplerate being 0\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=56427\n---END---\n2b84e859 2023-03-03 Write SANE extended zero to remove assert\nSimply ignoring this assert (as production code does) results in\nan endless loop.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=56323\n---END---\na336ea52 2023-02-25 Fix potential resource leak\n---END---\n285a3f55 2023-02-02 Split up writing metadata and comparing metadata into separate steps\nFor some reason it is possible to read and write in the same file\nwhen opened with fopen mode r+b on linux, but not on MacOS. Reading\nand 'verifying' is now split up into two steps, which does work.\nAdditional benefit is that all foreign metadata is written first,\nbefore verifying, which means as much data as possible is restored.\nThe error messages also more clearly state whether things went wrong\n--\ncc5c1d88 2006-10-06 complete WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE support, multichannel assignments in format and documentation, multichannel support for AIFF and WAVE, channel mapping, new --channel-map=none option to flac, saving and restoring of WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE channel mask to/from tag, robust handling of \"odd\" sample resolutions (i.e. not multiple of 8 bits) for AIFF and WAVE\n---END---\n825e72cf 2006-10-03 try to limit the #defines (of fseeko to fseek and ftello to ftell) to just the versions of MSVC that appear not to have fseeko()/ftello()\n---END---\nb292e75e 2006-09-14 add support for new REPLAYGAIN_REFERENCE_LOUDNESS tag\n---END---\n6b21f667 2006-09-13 merge down from merged-API-layer branch: cvs -q up -dP -j API_LAYER_MERGING_BASELINE -j API_LAYER_MERGING_BRANCH\n---END---\n7688f8e7 2006-07-07 MD5 comparison failures on decoding are now an error instead of a warning and will also return a non-zero exit code (SF #1493725).\n---END---\nd237379a 2006-07-06 change unparseable frame handling, from a fatal error and FLAC__STREAM_DECODER_UNPARSEABLE_STREAM state, to a soft error FLAC__STREAM_DECODER_ERROR_STATUS_UNPARSEABLE_STREAM; also fixup wave/aiff headers when -F and there is no STREAMINFO\n---END---\n48b1e6ec 2006-06-14 improve behavior of -F to decode even if there is no metadata\n---END---\nb1ec796b 2006-05-24 complete largefile support\n---END---\n0395dac1 2006-04-25 add 2206 to copyright notice\n---END---\n95e39a8f 2005-09-01 allow non-strict mode for reading replaygain tags, to fallback to track tags if album tags are not available and vice versa\n---END---\ne7001d6e 2005-08-24 change bug submission verbiage, require monitoring of sourceforge bug\n---END---\na78fac66 2005-01-25 add 2005 to copyright notices\n---END---\n1518d941 2005-01-07 better verbiage in bug-report lingo\n---END---\n49262508 2004-12-30 minor comments\n---END---\n07e00486 2004-11-12 minor error message fix\n--\ndde41029 2004-03-15 fix --until bug #851756\n---END---\n9564390f 2004-01-17 update copyright to 2004\n---END---\n0f220344 2003-12-17 fix endian bug when applying replaygain\n---END---\n1a698a88 2003-12-17 fix bug where apply gain is used on a file with no vorbis comment\n---END---\n99e8c2fa 2003-12-17 ugh, it's FLAC__ASSERT() not FLAC__assert()\n---END---\n3c5072c6 2003-12-17 use FLAC__assert() instead of assert()\n---END---\n9c650a56 2003-12-17 add undocumented option --apply-replaygain-which-is-not-lossless to flac; required a lot of reorganization; gain_analysis lib renamed to replaygain_analyis; replaygain_synthesis moved out of plugin_common into its own library in share/\n---END---\naf9c773d 2003-05-19 add Brady's better write_sane_extended()\n---END---\nafae69f0 2003-01-02 Add 2003 to copyright notice\n---END---\n1dfef453 2002-12-29 minor syntax\n---END---\nf91251d1 2002-12-28 add flushed fwrite in Valgrind mode\n---END---\n92cef3df 2002-12-17 add support for decoding to AIFF\n--\n04c594c1 2002-09-09 minor error message formatting\n---END---\n8304c8fd 2002-09-04 add support for serial number in Ogg streams\n---END---\neda534f2 2002-08-31 add checks for changing bps/sample_rate/channels mid-stream\n---END---\n1f99eac2 2002-08-23 fixes based on a pass over everything with autoconf/automake\n---END---\n09c35d2e 2002-08-08 code revamp finished\n---END---\n021cb51e 2002-08-07 beginning of code revamp, still broken\n---END---\nc80681f4 2002-08-07 use new ogg decoder from libOggFLAC\n---END---\ncfdfc828 2002-08-02 revamp decoder process calls",
